# LOCAL-EXPOSURE: UE Local Exposure (Bilateral) — grid + blurred log luminance, applied per pixel in the tonemap.
# Frames 1–2 are headless (the player opens only Projects/Desert): project = APFS clone
# DesertEngine-scratch/LOCAL-EXPOSURE/BistroClone, scenes B16_Bistro_Street.desce (identity) and _LE08.desce (0.8/0.8):
#   Editor --project <BistroClone>/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/B16_Bistro_Street{,_LE08}.desce
#          --camera 450,160,640 --look 0.5,0.1,-0.86 --shot-frames 90
#   Тогда 1_awning_before  shade under the awnings crushed and/or the street blown; identical to dev (identity)
#   Тогда 2_awning_after   awning interior readable, the street not blown, no halos at the awning edge
# Frame 3 is live, on the Desert project's Starter scene (its unbound PostProcessVolume 17921165617746467452).
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.LocalExposureHighlightContrastScale 0.8
Когда set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.LocalExposureShadowContrastScale 0.8
Тогда 2b_starter_lit Starter, Lit, Highlight/Shadow 0.8: the picture renders (no black/NaN), contrast slightly flatter
Когда run View "View mode: Local Exposure"
Тогда 3_visualize the Local Exposure view mode shows per-pixel exposure (not flat): shaded and lit areas differ
